  "subtitles": {
    "mode": "words",
    "words": "/Users/diplomat/ytvideos/new_channel/videos/037_cost_of_living/Work/ffmpeg_resume_20261104/forced_alignment.json",
    "transcript": "/Users/diplomat/ytvideos/new_channel/videos/037_cost_of_living/Source/Voice/en_v01_lawrence/voice_text_en.txt",
    "phrases": [
      "Bread. Fuel.",
      "Something to wash with.",
      "Something to light the room.",
      "Before the Black Death,",
      "a London labourer's yearly",
      "earnings cover",
      "only about three-quarters",
      "of the basic",
      "needs of a family of four.",
      "To pay for the full",
      "year's basket at that same",
      "daily rate would take roughly",
      "three hundred and thirty-three",
      "paid working days.",
      "But the model assumes",
      "only two hundred and fifty",
      "paid days in a year.",
      "That one annual",
      "wage falls short.",
      "Later, the same benchmark",
      "becomes much easier to cover.",
      "Then the daily wage more",
      "than doubles \u2014 and the basics",
      "move further away again.",
      "How much work did an ordinary",
      "year's necessities cost?",
      "Follow the price",
      "through the centuries,",
      "and the answer",
      "takes an unexpected turn.",
      "We will stay",
      "in London and compare",
      "a labourer's daily pay",
      "with the cost of basic needs.",
      "For the later periods,",
      "we follow building labourers,",
      "whose daily wages are lower",
      "than those of skilled",
      "building craftsmen.",
      "The yardstick",
      "is a reconstructed",
      "basic budget for a man,",
      "a woman and two children.",
      "It includes food, linen,",
      "soap, candles and fuel,",
      "with a small housing allowance.",
      "Think of an annual",
      "bill for a defined",
      "set of necessities.",
      "Divide that bill",
      "by a day's wage,",
      "and its price becomes",
      "a number of wage-days.",
      "A lower number",
      "means each day's pay",
      "buys more of the basket.",
      "These are price tags",
      "expressed in wages,",
      "rather than surviving records",
      "of anyone's working year.",
      "Families had different",
      "incomes and needs; employment",
      "could be interrupted.",
      "The calculation assumes",
      "two hundred and fifty",
      "paid days and adds",
      "only five percent for rent.",
